From b6f19b5dbcdba242196cb4435fc00b0b41879523 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:34:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Govern xai-oauth (Grok subscription) in the Kanban
 LLM pacing governor

Five whys: Grok (xai-oauth, X Ultra) was added to the pool-worker deep/standard model_routing classes
(state PR #3367, core PR #3301), but the pacing governor only judged anthropic and openai-codex. There
was no xai-oauth usage reader, so listing it would read `unknown` (fail open), and because `_governed`
skips any card with an ungoverned candidate provider, every class card whose routes include Grok, and
every Grok-pinned card, started ungoverned. Grok could absorb unbounded parallel runs until a 429 wall,
and this account has auto top-up on a saved payment method, so a drained pool spills into metered
Extra Usage.

Research (t_19ff0ce8c9b33e6a): api.x.ai response headers carry only per-minute RPS/TPM limits, but the
Grok subscription has one weekly usage pool, read by the official Grok Build CLI from
`GET https://cli-chat-proxy.grok.com/v1/billing?format=credits` with the OAuth bearer
(xai-org/grok-build xai-grok-shell/src/extensions/billing.rs). Live read from the hub's X Ultra row
2026-11-15: HTTP 200, currentPeriod USAGE_PERIOD_TYPE_WEEKLY (7 days), creditUsagePercent 2.0.

Change:
- agent/account_usage_xai.py: the reader. A weekly period maps to one account-scope `Current week`
  window (the governor's seven_day). Any other period type, or a missing percent, is unavailable
  (never headroom), so the pool stays `unknown` rather than being mis-paced. Only an OAuth token is
  sent, redirects are not followed, and the read-only variant never resolves or refreshes a login.
- agent/account_usage.py: register xai-oauth in the usage fetchers (normal and read-only).
- kanban.llm_pacing.providers default (+ PacingConfig): add xai-oauth.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_llm_pacing_xai.py, 12 tests. RED on origin/main 3f13528930 with
only the test file and the new reader module copied in: 4 fail (fetch_account_usage does not dispatch
xai-oauth, the redirect test, xai-oauth not in the default providers, and a Grok card at 90% weekly
starts instead of being held). GREEN on this branch: 12/12, plus the 38 test files that import
account_usage / kanban_llm_pacing (723 passed); scripts/check --base origin/main ok.
